# Tests (internal only — but TRACKED in the private DEV remote).
# Rationale: tests/ is the offline verification harness (smoke_*.py, the
# Chromium-judged multiscope corpus, parity snapshots). While untracked it was
# destroyed by a single `git clean -fdx`. Public exclusion is NOT enforced by
# this file: it is enforced by (a) the curated file-level release process — the
# public repo has an unrelated single-commit history, never a push of this tree
# — and (b) .git/hooks/pre-push, which blocks any ref whose tree contains
# tests/ from reaching a non-DEV BugTraceAI remote. tests/ is also excluded
# from Docker images by .dockerignore.
# Only harness SOURCE is tracked; generated artifacts stay ignored. To track a
# new non-source fixture type, add an explicit `!tests/**/*.<ext>` line.
tests/**
!tests/**/
!tests/**/*.py
!tests/**/*.md
tests/**/__pycache__/

# Dev scripts and archives (local-only)
scripts/
archive/
analyze_*.py
check_*.py
inspect_*.py
